  "source": {
    "title": "North Down Herald and County Down Independent, 17 January 1920, p. 1: \"Bangor Municipal Elections. Results of the Polling\" (Clifton Electoral Area). First names and initials: Northern Whig, 17 January 1920, p. 6 (\"Bangor\").",
    "publisher": "North Down Herald (via the British Newspaper Archive)",
    "kind": "news",
    "check": "the poll (488), invalid papers (8), quota (121), every first preference and the second count as printed; the first preferences add to the 480 valid votes, 480 / 4 + 1 = 121, and Thomson's surplus of 74 went 34 to M'Neill and 40 to Spence as printed. Thomson's 195 is read from a blurred figure, and is the only reading that gives 480",
    "confirmedBy": [
      "Bangor register of elections, typed result sheets of the 1920 count pasted in (PRONI LA/20/1/DA/1; Keep note \"LA/20/1/DA/1 Part 3\", #1 Clifton)"
    ]
  },
  "partyLabels": "none-recorded",
  "note": "Proportional representation (single transferable vote) under the Local Government (Ireland) Act 1919; polled 15 January 1920. Results declared 16 January 1920 by the returning officer, James Milliken (town clerk). The area returned 3 members. Thomson and M'Murray were elected on the first count; on the second count 34 of Thomson's surplus gave M'Neill exactly the quota. No report seen gives party labels.",
  "correctionNote": "The register's typed result sheet agrees with every figure; it gives 748 electors."
